<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Temiminó</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Temiminó were a Tupi-speaking Indigenous people of the coast of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanabara-bay">Guanabara Bay</a> and Espírito Santo, enemies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tupinamba">Tupinambá</a> allied with the French. Under their leader Arariboia they allied with the Portuguese and helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estacio-de-sa">Estácio de Sá</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mem-de-sa">Mem de Sá</a> drive the French out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> by 1567. In reward Arariboia received land across the bay, where the town of Niterói grew.</p></div>
